{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: RNA-only, singleprofile, PCA → 48.5% acc), the dominant uncertainty is whether the image modality carries any predictive signal at all. Before investing in multimodal fusion, multiprofile aggregation, or alternative encoders, I need a second unimodal baseline. config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is the cleanest possible comparison: it matches config_001 in simplicity (singleprofile, no aggregation, no fusion) and isolates the modality variable. If image accuracy substantially exceeds 48.5%, I know the image channel is the stronger signal and should prioritize image-centric and multimodal configurations. If it is comparable or lower, the problem is intrinsically difficult and I should focus on representation quality (encoder choice) rather than modality or fusion complexity. This single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about which modality to build upon, making it the highest-information next step under a tight budget."
}

